Z||000004||fiero56||03-24-2000||10:31 PM||||Just a few months ago, my Fiero hit the 150,000 mile mark. Even though it is a car that is meticulously maintained, everything is beginning to show its age: ball joints, fuel pump, a couple sensors, front and rear sway bar endlinks, etc. Plus wear items, brake components, tires, both tranny mounts and dogbone, etc. It was a perfect car at 149K, but now at 155K, it has a few issues.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||03-25-2000||12:54 AM||||I hear you, when my 85 GT hit 150k, lots of things suddenly started wearing out.||||reg||1
